          "severity": "major",
          "file": "frontend/src/hangar/assetPolicy.ts",
          "line": 225,
          "message": "The resource check still accepts a nested backslash-form location alongside a safe path. Reject backslashes in every resource-location field or validate each location before accepting the resource.",
          "confidence": 0.83,
          "category": "security",
          "evidence": {
            "codePathTraced": "The recursive resource scan checks strings for explicit URL schemes and counts known location keys per object, but it does not reject backslashes in every location field or validate nested location candidates. Only the top-level candidate reaches validateUri.",
            "failureScenario": "A caller validates `{ path: \"assets/model.glb\", metadata: { src: \"\\\\\\\\attacker.example/model.glb\" } }`. The safe top-level path passes; the nested src is not checked by validateUri, and its backslashes evade the scheme check. A consumer resolving that src can request the attacker origin. OWASP A01:2025."
          }
        }
      ]
    }
